/-!
# Local generation by `r` sections across `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a`, site by site

Let `S` be a scheme, `𝓕` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module and `r` a natural number.  Descent,
Lemma 05VG says that `𝓕` is locally generated by `r` sections (Modules on Sites,
Definition 03DL (4)) if and only if `𝓕^a` is locally generated by `r` sections as an `𝒪`-module,
at each of the comparison functors `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` of Descent, Proposition 03DX.  On both sides the
condition is `SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedByOnSite`: on the left it is read on the ringed
site of opens of `S`, on the right on the site carrying `𝓕^a`.

This file states that equivalence once for each site, with the topology a concrete constructor.

| site               | declaration                                                         |
|--------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `(Sch/S)_Zar`      | `isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_zariski`       |
| `(Sch/S)_étale`    | `isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_etale`         |
| `(Sch/S)_smooth`   | `isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_smooth`        |
| `(Sch/S)_syntomic` | `isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_syntomic`      |
| `(Sch/S)_fppf`     | `isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_fppf`          |
| `S_Zar`            | `isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_smallZariskiAssociatedModule`       |
| `S_étale`          | `isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_smallEtaleAssociatedModule`         |
| `S_smooth`         | `isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_smooth`   |
| `S_syntomic`       | `isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_syntomic` |
| `S_fppf`           | `isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_fppf`     |

All names are in the namespace `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_zariski` and
  its four siblings: the clause on the big site `(Sch/S)_τ`, at the functor
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModule`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_smallZariskiAssociatedModule` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_smallEtaleAssociatedModule`: the
  clause on `S_Zar` and on `S_étale`, at `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.associatedModule` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModule`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_fppf`
  and its two siblings: the clause on the small smooth, syntomic and fppf sites, at
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite.associatedModule`.

## Implementation notes

Each statement is specialised from a statement covering several sites at once, or restated
from the statement for its site:
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_baseAssociatedModule_iff` for every
topology of the big site,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_associatedModule` for every flat
small site, `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_associatedModule` on
`S_Zar` (where the comparison is an equivalence of ringed topoi, so that Modules on Sites,
Lemma 03DM applies and quasi-coherence is not needed) and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_associatedModule_iff` on `S_étale`.
None of them assumes an equivalence: the morphisms of ringed sites and topoi they use are
constructed, and every hypothesis on `𝓕` beyond quasi-coherence is proved.

The source's small sites are `S_Zar` and `S_étale`; the small smooth, syntomic and fppf sites are
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite`, whose objects are the schemes over `S` whose structure
morphism is smooth, syntomic, or flat and locally of finite presentation.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05VG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

public section

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG

/-! ### The big sites `(Sch/S)_τ` -/

section Big

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **Descent, Lemma 05VG, "locally generated by `r` sections", on `(Sch/S)_Zar`.**  A
quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module `𝓕` is locally generated by `r` sections if and only if `𝓕^a` is
locally generated by `r` sections as an `𝒪`-module on the big Zariski site of `S`. -/
@[stacks 05VG "locally generated by r sections, big site (Sch/S)_Zar"]
theorem isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_zariski (𝓕 : S.Modules)
    [𝓕.IsQuasicoherent] (r : ℕ) :
    SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedByOnSite (R := S.ringCatSheaf) 𝓕 r ↔
      SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedByOnSite
        ((BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModule B S hS .zariski).obj 𝓕) r :=
  BigFppfOver.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_baseAssociatedModule_iff B S hS .zariski 𝓕 r

